{
  "about": "Provenance of every third-party file under embedded/ (served from the binary at /_internal/*) and of the third-party files sdui.js loads from a CDN. TestEmbeddedThirdPartyManifest fails when a listed file's sha256 differs, a listed file is missing, or a file under embedded/ is neither listed here nor named in first_party. Each npm source was re-fetched on 2026-10-23, its sha512 matched the registry dist.integrity, and the embedded file is byte-identical to source_file in that tarball unless notes say otherwise.",
  "update_procedure": [
    "1. Choose the version from the registry metadata (https://registry.npmjs.org/<package>): the newest release in the current major unless the next major is a drop-in for the loader code. Check https://github.com/advisories?query=ecosystem%3Anpm+<package> for the target version.",
    "2. Download the tarball (dist.tarball) into a new, empty directory and verify its sha512 against dist.integrity before extracting. Never run npm install, package scripts or any code from the tarball.",
    "3. Copy source_file from the tarball verbatim to embedded/<path> (for a non-npm source, fetch the exact source URL). Do not rebuild or patch the file.",
    "4. Update version, source, source_file, registry_integrity, sha256 and size_bytes here. For mcp-apps also regenerate embedded/mcp-apps/VENDOR.json (its own refresh note). For a cdn_loaded file also update the URL and integrity in embedded/sdui.js and the URL constants in csp_cdn_sources.go.",
    "5. Check the consumers named in the entry's notes still use only APIs the new version keeps, then run: go test -tags sqlite_fts5 -run 'TestEmbeddedThirdParty|TestMCPAppsBundle|TestSDUILeaflet' ."
  ],
  "first_party": [
    "bm.js",
    "sdui.js",
    "markdown.js",
    "design.html",
    "THIRD_PARTY.json",
    "mcp-apps/VENDOR.json"
  ],
  "first_party_note": "Framework-authored files, plus the *_test.mjs Node tests (matched by suffix). design.html is not embedded in the binary.",
